  "worked_solution": "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-2t+\\operatorname{ln}\u2061t) \\\\  & =2t-2+\\frac{1}{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the velocity at $t=3,$ we substitute $t=3$ into the velocity function above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(3) & =2(3)-2+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =6-2+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{3} \\\\  & =4.333\\,333\u2026 \\\\  & \u22484.33\\end{aligned}\n$$",
